{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a57a4f1cfdcaa680","type":"text","text":"## **Big question**\nYou find a bottle labelled DRINK ME. What should you do?","x":450,"y":-335,"width":600,"height":112,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"5ffd9b445275378d","type":"text","text":"## **Learning goals**\n**I can:** identify the main idea; find **exactly two** dangers in the original text; use context clues; make a present perfect sentence; give safe advice using **should** and **could**.","x":450,"y":-195,"width":600,"height":154,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6f69a491fdf81573","type":"text","text":"**Starter, silence**\nWrite **one** advice sentence.\n\n**Context and prediction**\nRead the context note. Do **Q1**: *one sentence in English*.","x":450,"y":-10,"width":600,"height":195,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"8644e745cba01e0d","type":"text","text":"## **TASK before every answer**\n**T** Task: circle the instruction word.\n**A** Answer: letter, phrase or full sentence?\n**S** Special conditions: *exactly*, *copy*, *English*, *two*.\n**K** Keep checking: did you follow **all** instructions?\n\n**Reading focus:** skimming for the main idea, then scanning for **proof**.\n**Reading habit:** do not translate every word.\n**Voice level:** 0 for solo reading, 1 with your partner.","x":450,"y":218,"width":600,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a5f3b183d2c1a9ae","type":"text","text":"## **Original novel | Chapter I: Down the Rabbit-Hole**\n*Lewis Carroll, Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland (1865)*\n\n> It was all very well to say ‘Drink me,’ but the wise little Alice was not going to do that in a hurry.\n\n> ‘No, I'll look first,’ she said, ‘and see whether it's marked “poison” or not’; for she had read several nice little histories about children who had got burnt, and eaten up by wild beasts and other unpleasant things, all because they would not remember the simple rules their friends had taught them: such as, that a red-hot poker will burn you if you hold it too long; and that if you cut your finger very deeply with a knife, it usually bleeds; and she had never forgotten that, if you drink much from a bottle marked ‘poison,’ it is almost certain to disagree with you, sooner or later.\n\n> However, this bottle was not marked ‘poison,’ so Alice ventured to taste it, and finding it very nice, (it had, in fact, a sort of mixed flavour of cherry-tart, custard, pine-apple, roast turkey, toffee, and hot buttered toast,) she very soon finished it off.","x":1140,"y":-335,"width":830,"height":705},
		{"id":"d764d88a2943ed55","type":"text","text":"## **Context and vocabulary support**\nAlice has followed the White Rabbit. She finds a mysterious bottle and is deciding whether to drink from it.\n\n**Vocabulary Hints:**\n*poison* = gif; \n*ventured* = durfde.\n\n","x":1140,"y":403,"width":830,"height":198,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"4d1415d8d7fbed4a","type":"text","text":"**Read the original text once**\nFollow while the teacher reads. Then skim: what is this passage **mainly** about?\n\n**Q2:** choose **A, B or C**. Write only the letter.","x":2050,"y":-335,"width":630,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"59e81c9cdb91266e","type":"text","text":"** Reading detectives, pairs**\n**Q3:** copy **exactly TWO dangers** in short English phrases.\n**Q4:** explain **why** Alice reads the bottle label, in **ONE complete English sentence**.\n\nDecoder names the task; Evidence Finder points to the words. Swap roles.","x":2050,"y":-107,"width":630,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"73ab223da5196bab","type":"text","text":"**Meaning in context**\n**Q5:** decide what **Ventured** suggests and identify a clue.\n**Q6:** *actually* and *eventually* in . Choose the correct Dutch meanings.","x":2050,"y":151,"width":630,"height":174,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b9055ff710caa3cd","type":"text","text":"** Individual work**\n**Q7:** use **has + past participle** with *read*.\n**Q8:** give **TWO** pieces of safe advice: one with **should**, one with **could**.\n","x":2050,"y":354,"width":630,"height":218,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"83189d13ce56cb31","type":"text","text":"** Exit ticket: Q9**\nDid Alice leave the drink untouched?\nChoose **YES / NO** and copy **ONE short phrase** as evidence.","x":2050,"y":601,"width":630,"height":164,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"821ad29ddda2cf39","type":"text","text":"# Today's Class: Learning From the Novel\n### Alice in Wonderland | Lesson 1 of 3","x":-360,"y":-354,"width":650,"height":98,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"64d00e3b82c7e32d","type":"text","text":" \n### **10:05** - Introduction: the mystery bottle\n\n### **10:15**  Read and skim \n\n### **10:25**  Word meaning + false friends \n### **10:30 min**  Grammar + advice \n### **10:35 min**  Exit ticket ","x":-360,"y":-223,"width":650,"height":278,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"24d348ad87f0bab1","type":"text","text":"# **Homework** for the 26th of November\nUpload at least **2 unfamiliar words** in google classroom from the passage we discussed.\nWrite a **100-word note** advising Alice.","x":-360,"y":88,"width":650,"height":163,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"286bd664c670adb8","type":"text","text":"# **Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland**\n### Introducing the book | 2 VWO | 5 minutes","x":-2628,"y":-412,"width":650,"height":100,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"8229302e1c2dd474","type":"text","text":"##  Imagine you see a **white rabbit in a waistcoat checking a pocket watch**.\n\n### Would you **A. follow it**, **B. ignore it**, or **C. ask what is wrong**?\n\n","x":-2628,"y":-277,"width":650,"height":262,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"2c89c9139f02e935","type":"text","text":"## **Today’s big idea**\nWonderland is a world where ordinary rules often stop making sense.\n\n**Question:** How can curiosity help Alice, and when could it get her into trouble?","x":-2628,"y":24,"width":650,"height":195,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c2299590772c83b5","type":"text","text":"## **The book **\n- **Title:** *Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland*\n- **Author:** **Lewis Carroll**, the pen name of Charles Lutwidge Dodgson\n- **Published:** **1865**, in Victorian Britain\n- **Genre:** fantasy, humour and wordplay\n- **Main character:** Alice, a curious young girl","x":-1858,"y":-412,"width":670,"height":268,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a83317a35f2e293d","type":"text","text":"## **What happens? **\nAlice follows a **White Rabbit** down a rabbit hole into **Wonderland**.\n\nShe encounters odd characters, puzzling conversations and surprising changes.\n\n**This week’s chapters:**\n1. A mysterious bottle\n2. Advice from a Caterpillar\n3. A Mad Tea-Party","x":-1858,"y":-107,"width":670,"height":270,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"90203e2442e5560f","type":"text","text":"## **Why are we reading it? **\nYou will read **Carroll’s original English, not a simplified rewrite**.\n\nSome words and sentence structures are old-fashioned. That is okay.\n\n**Our reading tools:** predict, skim, scan, use context, and check what a question asks.\n\n **Open Lesson 1 in Google Classrooms.** What will Alice do with the bottle?","x":-1858,"y":198,"width":670,"height":276,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cf61704050fe6538","type":"text","text":"## **Our three 30-minute lessons**\n**Wednesday 25 Nov:** Down the Rabbit-Hole: curious or careful?\n\n**Thursday 26 Nov:** The Caterpillar: feelings and identity.\n\n**Friday 27 Nov:** The Mad Tea-Party: manners and advice.\n\nWe will also practise **health vocabulary, present perfect, modals, and TASK**.","x":-1088,"y":-412,"width":640,"height":295,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"01b2bc6422ec1e54","type":"text","text":"## **Reading rule**\nYou **do not** need to translate every word.\n\n1. Read for the overall meaning.\n2. Find the exact line that proves your answer.\n3. Decode instructions using **TASK**.\n\n**T** Task  **A** Answer  **S** Special conditions  **K** Keep checking","x":-1088,"y":-82,"width":640,"height":275,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"21fc7c35fa794e37","type":"text","text":"## **Ready to read?**\nA bottle says **DRINK ME**.\n\nWould you trust it?\n\nMake a prediction in **ONE English sentence** in your workbook (Lesson 1, Q1).","x":-1088,"y":223,"width":640,"height":220,"color":"1"}
	],
